Gnoll Jargon is the yipping, howling language of the hyena-folk known as
gnolls. It incorporates many sounds that civilized races find difficult to
reproduce, including high-pitched cackles, growling undertones, and barking
exclamations.

Native gnolls communicate complex tactical information and pack hierarchy
through subtle variations in pitch and tone that take years to master. Those
who learn even a basic understanding of Gnoll Jargon gain insight into these
savage hunters' communications.

This language proves useful when dealing with gnoll tribes, whether through
negotiation, espionage, or simply understanding their battle cries before
an ambush.

Class: General
Discipline: Advanced Adventuring

